The class `RectTools` contains the three static methods described below. You may not change any `Rectangle` object that is passed to a method.

```java
public class RectTools {
    /** Returns whichever of a and b has the greater area. If the areas are equal, returns a. */
    public static Rectangle larger(Rectangle a, Rectangle b)
    { /* to be implemented in part (a) */ }

    /** Returns a new Rectangle that could hold a on top of b: its width is the greater
     *  of the two widths and its height is the sum of the two heights. */
    public static Rectangle stacked(Rectangle a, Rectangle b)
    { /* to be implemented in part (b) */ }

    /** Returns a new Rectangle with the same shape as r (the same ratio of width to height)
     *  whose area is targetArea. Precondition: r.area() > 0 and targetArea > 0 */
    public static Rectangle scaleToArea(Rectangle r, double targetArea)
    { /* to be implemented in part (c) */ }
